# Pym Particles on Bot1's own Ornithopter: Bot1 draws a card (library 12 -> 11), the Ornithopter has vigilance and can't be blocked this turn, so
# Bot2's Ornithopter, a flier that could otherwise block it, may not (the refusal) and the attacker stays untapped. On turn five, with nothing done,
# the same attack can be blocked (the positive control) and taps, since "until end of turn" and "this turn" are over.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Pym Particles
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot1.Hand.Pym Particles.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Library.Count = 11
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Vigilance
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.CantBeBlocked = true
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.CantBeBlocked = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Pym Particles
